In article <C2Gs2q.6tx@skates.gsfc.nasa.gov> dc@cobi.gsfc.nasa.gov (Dave Cottingham) writes:
...
>a 386 with 2 meg of memory, and 560K of low memory free.  The MS-DOS
>is version 3.3.  I suspect that nethack is not finding any of the high
>memory.  Anyone know how to make nethack see that memory?

If by high memory you mean memory between 640K and 1Meg, the answer  is
you cant.  If you mean memory above 1Meg (aren't inconsistent naming
shemes a pain...), then NetHack will use it directly if it supports the
XMS protocol.  This is normally provided by HIMEM.SYS or 386MAX.

Assuming that you don't have any XMS providers, or they don't appear to 
work, then you want to provide a disk cache for the drive where 
nethack.exe resides.

